# OpenSpawn Python SDK

**Coordination layer for AI agent organizations.**

Define roles, hierarchy, and policies in a single markdown file. OpenSpawn handles task routing, credit budgets, escalations, and gives you a real-time dashboard.

This SDK lets you integrate OpenSpawn into Python-based agent frameworks like **CrewAI**, **LangGraph**, or **AutoGen**.

## Installation

```bash
pip install openspawn
```

## Quick Start

```python
from openspawn import OpenSpawn, TaskPriority

# Initialize client
client = OpenSpawn(
    api_url="https://api.openspawn.ai",  # or your self-hosted instance
    api_key="your-api-key",
    org_id="your-org-id"
)

# Create a task
task = client.tasks.create(
    title="Build new feature",
    description="Implement user authentication",
    priority=TaskPriority.HIGH,
    assignee_agent_id="engineer-1"
)

# List tasks
tasks = client.tasks.list(status="pending")
for task in tasks:
    print(f"{task.title} - {task.status}")

# Update task status
client.tasks.transition(task.id, status="in_progress")

# List agents
agents = client.agents.list()
for agent in agents:
    print(f"{agent.name} (L{agent.level} {agent.role})")

# Send a message
client.messages.send(
    content="Feature deployed!",
    channel_id="engineering"
)

# Check credit balance
balance = client.credits.balance("engineer-1")
print(f"Balance: {balance.balance} credits")
```

## Integration with CrewAI

```python
from crewai import Agent, Task, Crew
from openspawn import OpenSpawn

# Wrap CrewAI with OpenSpawn coordination
client = OpenSpawn(org_id="my-crew")

# Define agents
engineer = Agent(
    role="Senior Engineer",
    goal="Build features",
    backstory="10 years of Python experience"
)

# Create corresponding OpenSpawn agent
client.agents.register(
    name="engineer-1",
    role="Senior Engineer",
    level=6,  # L6 = Senior
    domain="engineering"
)

# When you create a CrewAI task, mirror it in OpenSpawn
crew_task = Task(description="Build auth", agent=engineer)
openspawn_task = client.tasks.create(
    title="Build auth",
    assignee_agent_id="engineer-1",
    priority="high"
)

# Run crew
crew = Crew(agents=[engineer], tasks=[crew_task])
result = crew.kickoff()

# Mark complete in OpenSpawn
client.tasks.transition(openspawn_task.id, status="done")
```

## Integration with LangGraph

```python
from langgraph.graph import StateGraph
from openspawn import OpenSpawn

client = OpenSpawn(org_id="my-langgraph-org")

# Define your LangGraph workflow
workflow = StateGraph(...)

# Wrap nodes to report to OpenSpawn
def engineering_node(state):
    task = client.tasks.create(
        title="Process engineering request",
        assignee_agent_id="engineer-agent"
    )
    
    # Do work
    result = do_engineering_work(state)
    
    # Mark done
    client.tasks.transition(task.id, status="done")
    return result

workflow.add_node("engineer", engineering_node)
```

## API Reference

### `OpenSpawn(api_url, api_key, org_id, timeout=30)`

Main client class.

**Environment variables:**
- `OPENSPAWN_API_KEY` — API key
- `OPENSPAWN_ORG_ID` — Organization ID

### `client.tasks`

- `create(title, description, priority, assignee_agent_id)` → Task
- `list(status=None, assignee_agent_id=None)` → list[Task]
- `get(task_id)` → Task
- `transition(task_id, status)` → Task
- `assign(task_id, assignee_agent_id)` → Task

### `client.agents`

- `list()` → list[Agent]
- `get(agent_id)` → Agent
- `register(name, role, level)` → Agent

### `client.messages`

- `send(content, channel_id=None, recipient_agent_id=None)` → Message
- `list(channel_id, limit=50)` → list[Message]

### `client.credits`

- `balance(agent_id)` → CreditBalance

### `client.escalations`

- `list_open()` → list[Escalation]
- `resolve(escalation_id)` → Escalation

## Models

All API responses are returned as dataclass instances:

- `Agent` — Agent metadata (id, name, role, level, domain, trust_score)
- `Task` — Task data (id, title, status, priority, assignee)
- `TaskStatus` — Enum: pending, claimed, in_progress, review, done, failed, cancelled
- `TaskPriority` — Enum: critical, high, medium, low
- `Channel` — Message channel
- `Message` — Chat message
- `CreditBalance` — Agent credit balance
- `Escalation` — Task escalation

